  "ground_truth": {
    "root_cause": "A modest latency increase in payments-api (read-replica lag pushed p95 from ~90ms to ~400ms) triggered aggressive retries from checkout-api's payments client, which had no backoff and no retry budget. Retry amplification roughly 5x'd checkout-api's outbound request volume, which exhausted its database connection pool and then its worker thread pool, turning a minor downstream slowdown into a checkout outage.",
    "evidence_path": [
      "payments-api p95 latency rises from ~90ms to ~400ms at 09:15 due to read-replica lag",
      "checkout-api logs slow payments-api calls, then 'retrying ... no backoff or retry budget' at 09:19",
      "checkout-api outbound request rate climbs from ~120/s to ~640/s (retry amplification)",
      "checkout-api DB connection pool exhausted at 09:21 (waiters=140) and pool wait time spikes",
      "checkout-api worker thread pool exhausted -> HTTP 503 at 09:23",
      "no deploys occurred in the window; recovery follows the operator cutting the retry budget"
    ],
    "fix": "Add exponential backoff with jitter and a retry budget / circuit breaker to checkout-api's payments-api client, isolate the connection pool used for downstream calls, and add load shedding. Separately, address the payments-api read-replica lag.",
    "should_escalate": false
  }
}
